1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,080
In Super Mario 64,

2
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:03,560
a character appears carrying a camera.

3
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:06,720
Mario and the camera have separate controls.

4
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:08,800
We will look closely, circle around,

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,880
and pull back, in that order.

6
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:14,080
The camera follows Mario.

7
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:17,080
The C buttons change its position and direction.

8
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:19,760
The viewpoint is where we see the scene from.

9
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:23,240
Turn the viewpoint to look around and upward.

10
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:25,920
It helps you find routes and Power Stars.

11
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:27,200
Think about where Mario stands

12
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,360
separately from what the camera points toward.

13
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:32,960
C-up enters a close view.

14
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:35,480
The stick now looks around.

15
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:39,140
Press A, B, or a C button other than C-up

16
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:41,040
to return to movement control.

17
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:43,720
Press C-left or C-right.

18
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:45,840
The camera circles Mario.

19
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:48,280
See the same Mario from another side.

20
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:49,680
When the camera cannot go farther,

21
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:51,920
a buzz signals its limit.

22
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:53,800
Press C-down

23
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:55,560
to pull the camera back.

24
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:57,200
Mario looks smaller.

25
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,240
More surroundings fit in view.

26
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:01,920
Look closely, circle around, and pull back.

27
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:03,100
In Super Mario 64,

28
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:05,200
the player is also the cinematographer.
